## Summary

Docs for Project Hive Phase 3 ([#1316](https://github.com/openJiuwen-ai/DigitalMate/issues/1316) steps 3.1–3.7, design [#1228](https://github.com/openJiuwen-ai/DigitalMate/issues/1228), acceptance [#1314](https://github.com/openJiuwen-ai/DigitalMate/issues/1314)).

**Hive 3 constituent.** It will land through `hive/hive3-integration`, which is cut after G4 ([#1421](https://github.com/openJiuwen-ai/DigitalMate/pull/1421)). Do not merge to main directly.

- **Phase 3 delivery design** (`docs/implementations/contracts/beebou-hive-phase3-delivery.md`):
  - work packages and gates;
  - what starts before G4 and what waits for it;
  - the integration model;
  - scheme two restated for SC04-A4, SC04-E1, the client fixtures and SC05-M5;
  - the G5 evidence model;
  - the real test environment and emulator;
  - the cutover path to G6;
  - open owner sign-offs.
- **ADR-0023** records the seven coordination decisions (D1–D7) and the alternatives rejected. Product semantics stay with #1228 and ADR-0022.
- **H-R1–H-R16 legacy Router caller inventory** (`docs/implementations/migration/hive-legacy-router-inventory.md`) on main `0ce02a22`:
  - per row: the definitions, per-class hit counts and every production caller with `path:line`;
  - a summary of what still blocks each delete condition;
  - baseline for #1313 step 3.6; G6 reruns it.
  - The coordinator re-checked it on the same SHA. 308 of 361 references resolve as written; the rest are short paths under `agent_bridge/src`. 45 of 47 definition rows name the symbol on the stated line; the other two are an import alias and a module row. Spot checks of H-R1, H-R5, H-R7 and the `server.router` importers match.
- Index and `UPDATES.md` entries in `adrs/`, `contracts/` and `migration/`.

The design page and ADR link `docs/guides/operations/hive-test-env-deploy.md`. That runbook comes from the parallel deploy lane's PR, and both meet in `hive/hive3-integration`.

